Here's the MATLAB code for a function that calculates the profit earned from the sales of an item based on its cost, selling price, and the number of units sold while ensuring a minimum profit margin of 10%:
```
function [total_profit] = calculate_profit(cost, selling_price, units_sold)
    % Calculate the profit margin
    profit_margin = (selling_price - cost) / selling_price;

    % Check if the profit margin is less than the minimum required
    if profit_margin < 0.1
        % Adjust the selling price to meet the minimum profit margin
        selling_price = cost / (1 - 0.1);
    end

    % Calculate the total profit
